    "updated_at": "2016-04-07T20:42:23Z",
    "body": "@owencm The flow you suggest could work, although it is definitely a UX regression compared to what we currently achieve with chrome.usb due to step 2 \"User clicks notification\".  Significantly, this also means the users must unlock their computer, turning a 2 second passive task (drop wearable into charging cradle) into a longer interactive task (wake up screen saver, enter password, wait for or seek out the popup, click it)\n@reillyeon Yes that sounds like a workable permission model to achieve UX parity. Presumably this would be added to \"Content Settings > USB Device\" to allow the user to revoke the permission if needed.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
